  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.1. Increased capacity of member States to create an enabling environment for entrepreneurship and sustainable enterprises</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In June 2021, the Ministry of Labour, Employment Opportunity and Youth Affairs; the Vereniging Surinaams Bedrijfsleven (VSB) / Suriname Trade and Industry Association (STIA); and Raad van Vakcentrales / Council of Trade Unions in Suriname (RAVAKSUR) adopted a tripartite action plan aimed at improving the national business landscape and increase productivity. It has four pillars: adequate social protection, social dialogue, education training and learning for life, and information communication and technology. The document is based on the findings of a report that captured tripartite constituents&#x2019; general perceptions of the business environment and its potential effect on productivity in Suriname. It also explores the initial impact of the pandemic on the business environment and its possible impacts in the future. The report was presented for comments to the tripartite partners in December 2020 and validated and adopted on 24 May 2021. Between 2020 and 2021, the ILO supported constituents in Suriname in articulating and finalizing the action plan based on key priorities coming out from the Enabling Environment for Sustainable Enterprise (EESE) report and taking into account the current context of the COVID 19 crisis. This included the preparation and delivery of presentations on the key findings of the Enabling Environment for Sustainable Enterprises and Productivity report (based on an ILO&#x2019;s methodology); compilation and organization of key discussion points on the priorities and action planning; and tripartite consultations.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">4.1.1. Number of member States with a strategy and/or action plan to improve the enabling environment for sustainable enterprises&#x2019; creation and growth</narrative>
